*> PLB-C100 table-keys-unsorted: a SEARCH ALL table whose start value,
*> from VALUE clauses, is out of its KEY order.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. UNSORTED.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
*> Reported: 03 after 05.
01  WS-STATES-V.
    05  FILLER          PIC X(7) VALUE "01ALPHA".
    05  FILLER          PIC X(7) VALUE "05BETA ".
    05  FILLER          PIC X(7) VALUE "03GAMMA".
01  WS-STATES REDEFINES WS-STATES-V.
    05  WS-STATE OCCURS 3 ASCENDING KEY WS-STATE-CODE INDEXED BY WS-SX.
        10  WS-STATE-CODE   PIC X(2).
        10  WS-STATE-NAME   PIC X(5).
*> Reported: numbers, DESCENDING, 7 before 9.
01  WS-RATES-V.
    05  FILLER          PIC 9(3) VALUE 9.
    05  FILLER          PIC 9(3) VALUE 7.
    05  FILLER          PIC 9(3) VALUE 9.
01  WS-RATES REDEFINES WS-RATES-V.
    05  WS-RATE OCCURS 3 DESCENDING KEY WS-RATE-KEY INDEXED BY WS-RX.
        10  WS-RATE-KEY     PIC 9(3).
*> Not reported: in order; AA before 11, which only ASCII puts first.
01  WS-CODES-V.
    05  FILLER          PIC X(2) VALUE "AA".
    05  FILLER          PIC X(2) VALUE "11".
    05  FILLER          PIC X(2) VALUE "22".
01  WS-CODES REDEFINES WS-CODES-V.
    05  WS-CODE OCCURS 3 ASCENDING KEY WS-CODE-KEY INDEXED BY WS-CX.
        10  WS-CODE-KEY     PIC X(2).
01  WS-WANT             PIC X(2) VALUE "03".
01  WS-WANT-N           PIC 9(3) VALUE 7.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    SEARCH ALL WS-STATE
        AT END DISPLAY "NONE"
        WHEN WS-STATE-CODE(WS-SX) = WS-WANT
            DISPLAY WS-STATE-NAME(WS-SX)
    END-SEARCH
    SEARCH ALL WS-RATE
        WHEN WS-RATE-KEY(WS-RX) = WS-WANT-N
            DISPLAY "RATE"
    END-SEARCH
    SEARCH ALL WS-CODE
        WHEN WS-CODE-KEY(WS-CX) = WS-WANT
            DISPLAY "CODE"
    END-SEARCH
    STOP RUN.
